{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Configure node1's local password authentication so an account locks after five failed login attempts.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final PAM/authselect configuration is valid and enables faillock with local_users_only and deny=5. A fresh local account authenticated successfully, accumulated exactly one record for each of five failed password attempts, and then rejected the correct password while locked.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e49705b282af4142","cmd-eb0aefba92034fba","cmd-3c47f978fc0a4578","cmd-5efa62a616c24712","cmd-719bb7e5c6ec4e3d"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Keep the account locked for five minutes and then automatically restore password access.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The effective unlock_time is 300 seconds. After demonstrating the locked state, a timed probe using the correct password succeeded after 305 seconds and showed an empty failure ledger, directly demonstrating automatic recovery.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5efa62a616c24712","cmd-740f8b1e83f3405b","cmd-6288d3a674c5486d","cmd-719bb7e5c6ec4e3d"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.99,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The authselect and faillock changes were required, while the probe account, credentials, known-host entry, timeout helper, and failure records were bounded verification artifacts that were reset and removed. The reboot timer served the mandatory restart protocol and disappeared across reboot. Final and lifecycle checks show no probe account, failed units, extra listeners, package damage, or non-system temporary residue. The retained faillock rollback backup has a clear recovery role and is not treated as unnecessary.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e49705b282af4142","cmd-ec1a9685bc6546dc","cmd-72aea7a5d70b42ea","cmd-740f8b1e83f3405b","cmd-532f5edc38674e85","cmd-d8293b57d6d74da1","cmd-11bbd79f0d7542ab","cmd-719bb7e5c6ec4e3d","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: node1 was healthy before restart, acknowledged the restart, returned with a different boot identity corroborated by lifecycle observations, recovered SSH and policy state, and passed the five-attempt lockout test again.","limitations":["The timeout test checked recovery after 305 seconds but did not probe immediately before the 300-second boundary; exact duration is therefore supported jointly by the effective unlock_time=300 configuration and the observed locked-to-recovered transition.","Some numeric authentication return-code text was redacted, though visible denial/success output, failure ledgers, explicit assertions, and zero command exits preserve the behavioral result.","Lifecycle snapshots do not inventory /root, so they do not independently confirm the final presence or absence of the rollback file created by cmd-ec1a9685bc6546dc; no later command removes it."]}
